  <h1>About</h1>

  <h2>Background</h2>
  <p>I am a software engineer with a background in backend and systems development.</p>
  <p>
    My work has involved building server-side components, designing service interfaces, and working with C++ and Linux-based systems.
  </p>
  <p>
    I am interested in how software systems are structured, how components communicate, and how engineering decisions affect reliability and maintainability.
  </p>

  <h2>Engineering Approach</h2>
  <p>I care about clear system boundaries, explicit interfaces, and predictable failure handling.</p>
  <p>When designing a system, I pay particular attention to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Module responsibilities and ownership</li>
    <li>Communication protocols and data flow</li>
    <li>Concurrency and asynchronous execution</li>
    <li>Failure handling and system observability</li>
    <li>Performance and maintainability</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Current Focus</h2>
  <p>My current technical interests include:</p>
  <h3>AI Systems</h3>
  <p>Exploring agent architectures, model integration, real-time voice systems, and AI-powered applications.</p>
  <h3>Intelligent Hardware</h3>
  <p>Studying the interaction between embedded devices, edge computing, cloud services, and AI applications.</p>
  <h3>Robotics Software</h3>
  <p>Learning and experimenting with ROS 2, robotics middleware, and the software architecture of intelligent machines.</p>

  <h2>Technical Interests</h2>
  <p>C++ · Linux · Distributed Systems · Networking · AI Infrastructure · ROS 2 · Edge Computing</p>
